# Cloud Agent PR Screenshots

When a **Cloud Agent** creates or updates a pull request (via
`ManagePullRequest`), the PR body must include a **before and after**
screenshot section so reviewers can see the visual impact at a glance.

## Never commit screenshots to git

Screenshots and recordings belong **only in the PR description**, not in
the repository. They must not appear in Files changed.

- **Do not** `git add` or commit PNGs, JPGs, WebPs, GIFs, or videos used
  for PR review (including `docs/pr-screenshots/`, `screenshots/`,
  `*.before.png`, `*.after.png`).
- **Do not** add `/opt/cursor/artifacts/` or any screenshot folder to the
  repo.
- **Do not** link the PR body at branch-raw paths like
  `.../raw/<branch>/docs/pr-screenshots/...` — that requires committing
  the files.
- Save captures under `/opt/cursor/artifacts/screenshots/` and embed them
  with `<img>` tags. `ManagePullRequest` uploads them to GitHub and
  rewrites the URLs.

```markdown
# ❌ BAD — files land in the repo
![after](docs/pr-screenshots/after-home.png)
git add docs/pr-screenshots/

# ✅ GOOD — description only
<img alt="Home after" src="/opt/cursor/artifacts/screenshots/home-after.png" width="400" />
```

## When required

- **UI, layout, styling, copy, or animation changes** — before and after
  screenshots are **required**.
- **Non-visual changes** (API-only, config, tests, docs with no rendered
  output) — omit the screenshots section and briefly note why (e.g.
  "No visual changes").

## Capturing screenshots

1. **Before** — Capture the current state *before* your changes:
   - For rebuild/parity work, screenshot the live reference page
     (https://www.mariamecoulibaly.com/) or the relevant route on the
     running dev build checked out at the PR base branch.
   - Save to `/opt/cursor/artifacts/screenshots/<descriptive-name>-before.png`.
2. **After** — Run the dev app with your branch, navigate to the same
   route/viewport, and capture the updated state.
   - Save to `/opt/cursor/artifacts/screenshots/<descriptive-name>-after.png`.
3. Use the same viewport width and page scroll position for both shots so
   the comparison is meaningful (default to desktop ~1280px unless the
   change is mobile-specific).
4. Prefer still screenshots for the before/after pair. Use screen
   recording (`RecordScreen`) only when motion or interaction is the
   primary change — link the video separately in the walkthrough.

## PR body format

Include a **Screenshots** section near the top of the PR description (after
the summary, before technical notes). Reference artifacts with absolute paths
in HTML `<img>` tags — `ManagePullRequest` uploads them and rewrites URLs
for GitHub:

```markdown
## Summary

Brief description of what changed and why.

## Screenshots

| Before | After |
|--------|-------|
| <img alt="About page before" src="/opt/cursor/artifacts/screenshots/about-before.png" width="400" /> | <img alt="About page after" src="/opt/cursor/artifacts/screenshots/about-after.png" width="400" /> |

## Walkthrough

Optional notes on how to verify, edge cases, or links to screen recordings.
```

Use descriptive `alt` text and filenames (e.g. `home-hero-before.png`,
`project-card-hover-after.png`).

## Checklist before opening the PR

- [ ] Before screenshot captured from base/reference state
- [ ] After screenshot captured from your branch with the dev app running
- [ ] Both images saved under `/opt/cursor/artifacts/screenshots/`
- [ ] PR body includes the Screenshots section with `<img>` tags
- [ ] Same viewport and route used for both shots
- [ ] No screenshot or recording files staged or committed

When **updating** an existing PR after further visual changes, refresh the
after screenshot (and the before shot if the baseline changed).
